# Short lines in CURSOR.md and ADRs

Governs `CURSOR.md` and `docs/architecture/*.md` only.

Never write long sentences in those files.

One numbered title, then short sub-items. Do not pack a paragraph of facts into a single line.

```markdown
6. Bindings
 1. One Wails struct per pane under `bindings/`.
 2. `App` keeps Start/Stop and OBS HTTP.
 3. `AppVersion` is stamped at link time.
```

Do not:

```markdown
6. **Bindings**: GetSettings / SaveSettings, GetOBSStatus, Start / Stop … (rest of the contract in one sentence)
```

Tables, code fences, and the intended-tree listing may stay wide. Prose and bullet items stay short.

# Stable numbered lists

Do not edit a line that is still correct.

Do not insert a new numbered sub-item in the middle of a list.

That renumbers every later item. The git diff then looks like a large rewrite.

Append the new sub-item at the end. Leave existing numbers unchanged.
